      "message": "Per discussion, we\u0027re thinking of the following:\n- Make close() throw no exceptions\n- Extend closeable instead of autocloseable\n- Use an AtomicInteger to store the fd. close would do \"int fd \u003d mFd.getAndSet(-1); close(fd)\", and other methods would just call get(), and if the fd ends up being -1, or if the map was closed from another thread, just do the wrong thing. This seems better for performance.\n- Put the reachability fences in all the methods, because otherwise it\u0027s possible for the finalizer to run concurrently with code that uses the map.",
